WEBVTT

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:12.360
Both of you, thank you
for coming with me.

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:16.120
But... you would've been
better off staying in Tokyo.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.020
Idiot!

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.270
We couldn't let you go alone, could we?

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.250
Sitting around...

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:25.000
won't accomplish anything, will it?

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:27.280
Y-Yeah, that's right.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.130
I knew it during the second battle:

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:34.720
Byakko's a lot stronger
than the other demons.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.670
M-My Poltergeist is--

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.880
It's not like this is a contest.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.630
Yeah, but still...

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:44.340
Oh, look!

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.840
I bought something at the Demon Auction!

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.380
Huh? Bought with money?

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.350
I don't really know.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:53.220
But these numbers have gone down.

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:56.580
It scared me at first,
and I didn't like it,

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:02.200
but this power lets me protect
people and fight our enemies.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:04.710
No matter what happens...

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:07.520
I'll protect you both.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:08.780
Huh?

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:07.350
The bureau chief told us about you.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:08.620
Thank you for coming.

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:10.990
Welcome to Osaka!

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:15.840
You all are the Summoners
assigned to Tokyo, huh?

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.130
We've been waitin'.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:19.550
Who are you?

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.930
I'm Hinako Kujo. And...

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.760
Over there's Keita Wakui.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:30.760
Like you all, they're Summoners
assigned just yesterday.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:32.410
The same, huh?

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.190
N-Nice to meet you.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:39.020
If you all are lookin' for someone,
do it on yer own!

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:40.530
Hey, Keita!

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:42.480
My job is...

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:45.410
Demon hunting.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:50.210
What's with him?

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:55.090
Well, that kid ain't too scared
of our situation, huh?

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:57.530
He's a dangerous one.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:13.300
Search teams have gone out
lookin' several times already...

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:16.480
Anyway, I'll show ya. Prof. Kanno's lab.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:22.200
The room's stayed as-is since
the professor disappeared.

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:28.540
So, this desk was the last one
to have seen the professor.

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:31.610
Have you been able to find any clues?

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:32.970
Not at all.

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:35.510
Not even any signs of a struggle.

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:39.160
Hell, there's not even a trace of
her leavin' the building.

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:51.930
Jeez. Lookin' for people
without any clues?

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:56.440
What a waste. I mean,
the enemy's out there.

00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:58.110
We oughta just...

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:01.260
kill 'em all.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:12.180
A demon!

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:16.670
We're Summoners now, huh?

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:20.120
Aren't there more
Summoner-like jobs for us?

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:23.800
Daichi's right.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:28.360
Maybe there's another reason
we've been sent here.

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:33.020
That man.

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:36.170
For him to come right to us...

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:37.850
How interesting.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:41.820
It's not like I'm taking your side.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:46.820
I just wish to further
test the humans...

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:52.150
What's going on?

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:54.730
The barrier system is being
attacked from the outside!

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:55.410
What did you say?

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:57.700
This is JP's main bureau!

00:05:57.700 --> 00:05:59.230
There's no way they could do that!

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:00.750
Still, we're clearly...!

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:05.660
JP's lines have every
form of protection,

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:07.630
and are infused with magical defenses!

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:08.850
It's impossible!

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:15.300
What's going on?!

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:16.630
Try using another line.

00:06:16.630 --> 00:06:17.260
It's no good!

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:19.600
At this rate, the system
will be overridden!

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:21.980
Initiate defense programs!

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:24.430
Don't let some cracker get in here!

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:25.150
Sir!

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:42.740
Find out where that cracker's located!

00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:45.800
Beginning a traceback of the
network intrusion path.

00:06:49.790 --> 00:06:52.330
What gives? What's all the ruckus?

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:59.470
Layer 1 Lloigor is down!

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:03.590
The password was cracked magically!

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:08.650
So this is, what? A
hacker attack, right?

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:10.940
This feels kinda dangerous.

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:11.870
Layer 2 is down!

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:15.200
Are the Septentrion behind this, too?

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:18.060
Who are you?

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:20.320
Hibiki Kuze, a Summoner.

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:21.880
The one from Tokyo.

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:25.080
They had this kid join JP's?

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:27.380
What is the bureau chief thinking?

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:31.040
This doesn't concern you all. Fall back.

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:32.430
It DOES concern us!

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:34.420
"Fall back"?

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:36.010
There's nowhere to run, is there?

00:07:37.110 --> 00:07:38.610
The third layer is down!

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.430
So, wouldn't it be better to
disconnect the network?

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:47.970
Just cuttin' the... Oh, thanks.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:51.140
Just cuttin' the power
would do it, right?

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:53.130
We can't do something that foolish!

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:58.690
If we cut this system, Osaka would
instantly lose all magical protection.

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:02.260
We'd be defenseless
against the intruders!

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:07.030
Maybe someone... is
helping the Septentrion.

00:08:07.030 --> 00:08:08.300
It could be.

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:11.540
Someone else is targeting us, huh?

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:14.330
This is no accident.

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:18.310
Yamato Hotsuin knew that this
would happen, didn't he?

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:20.380
The fourth layer is down!

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:22.020
Finished tracing the cracker's location!

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:26.850
So, it's somewhere close by?

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:31.610
What is this?

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:34.280
The attacks are from all over Japan!

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:37.190
What? Most of our networks are dead.

00:08:37.190 --> 00:08:38.450
This can't be!

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:40.370
This is a diversion.
Get me specifics, stat!

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:42.440
Now what, at a time like this?

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:46.410
A new "dead face" clip has arrived.

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:54.630
Keita!

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:55.540
Huh?

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:57.150
Keita! It's Keita!

00:08:57.850 --> 00:08:59.880
Kujo, do you know that place?

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:01.210
Who cares about the place?!

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:01.920
Please!

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:06.770
That...

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:10.980
It's Festival Gate.
It's pretty close by.

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:14.150
Hurry! Limit the location
to someplace near here.

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:16.660
What do you know, boy? Keep quiet.

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:17.810
Hurry!

00:09:17.810 --> 00:09:18.590
Okay.

00:09:23.150 --> 00:09:27.410
Search complete. It's
Osaka, Naniwa Ward.

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:28.750
The abandoned Festival Gate park.

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:32.080
That's where the cracker
is hitting us from.

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:35.510
He's that close?

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:38.790
Awesome, Hibiki. How did you know?

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:39.930
I thought so...

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:42.140
There, eh?

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:45.560
Hibiki Kuze. You're there, yes?

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:47.630
Bureau Chief!

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:51.500
Head for Festival Gate and
stop that cracker at once.

00:09:52.010 --> 00:09:54.270
Other nearby Summoners should go, too.

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:55.570
Um...

00:09:56.680 --> 00:10:00.870
Did you send us here knowing
this could happen?

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:06.120
...to the abandoned Festival Gate
in Naniwa Ward at once.

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:10.130
There's not a moment to
lose. Hurry up and go.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:14.200
All those able--

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:15.250
Excuse me.

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:19.960
Please order Keita Wakui
to not go that location.

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:23.420
The "dead face" clips show the future.

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:26.620
If we can see it, we can avoid it.

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:55.240
Who's that?! Friggin' startled me.

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:02.550
I can't get through.

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:04.560
Please make it in time.

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:18.340
Bastard!

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:26.790
Berserk!

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:54.320
Hibiki Kuze, Daichi Shijima,
Io Nitta, Hinako Kujo.

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:56.480
The four of them will shortly
storm Festival Gate.

00:11:56.950 --> 00:12:00.500
Additionally, eight Summoners in
the Osaka area are on their way.

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:02.940
They can rendezvous with them
in about three minutes.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:04.990
Go, Berserk!

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:22.800
There's no end to them.

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:34.260
You weak chumps stick together.

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:35.730
Whoa!

00:12:50.690 --> 00:12:51.290
Lilim!

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:56.250
Keita!

00:12:56.700 --> 00:12:59.250
Hinako? What gives? Why're you here?

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:03.380
Idiot! If I hadn't come, you'd be dead!

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:05.120
Mind yer business!

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:07.890
I thought you guys were looking
for that professor chick!

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:09.810
Keita, behind you!

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:18.860
Keita!

00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:22.320
Mister Keita to you. Have some respect!

00:13:23.060 --> 00:13:25.820
I'm glad we made it. You okay?

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:27.110
Huh?

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:29.690
Yeah. How long you gonna hold me?!

00:13:31.650 --> 00:13:32.750
Anyway...

00:13:33.190 --> 00:13:35.040
If we don't hurry and find the
cell phone that's run amok,

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:36.880
these things won't stop poppin' up!

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:41.700
No. A cracker is controlling these.

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:42.210
Huh?

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:44.330
I'll look for him.

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:46.800
Let's go, my new demons!

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:50.750
Obariyon! Agathion! Go help out Byakko!

00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:52.460
They okay?

00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:53.810
Leave it to them.

00:13:57.420 --> 00:14:00.400
M-My demons are weak!

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:03.010
You there, Hibiki?

00:14:03.390 --> 00:14:05.150
Yes! And the other Summoners?

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:07.420
Huh?

00:14:08.630 --> 00:14:13.330
Unfortunately... You're the only
ones to have made it there yet.

00:14:18.220 --> 00:14:21.700
No matter. Hurry and take
the cracker into custody.

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:22.710
But...!

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:28.720
The cracker is hiding about 50 meters
from your current location.

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:32.680
We have to catch the bad guy, right?

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:33.850
I'll go look!

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:36.480
Understood.

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:39.270
Hinako and I will hold back the enemies.

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:40.150
Okay!

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:41.940
I'M here, too! Don't forget 'bout me!

00:14:42.220 --> 00:14:43.400
And me?

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:44.760
You protect Nitta.

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:45.530
Yes!

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:46.940
Let's go.

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:47.990
Yeah!

00:14:48.470 --> 00:14:49.910
Go, Byakko!

00:14:52.150 --> 00:14:53.230
Lilim!

00:15:03.610 --> 00:15:04.840
Layer 6 is down!

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:07.290
What about our counterattack program?

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:08.550
It's having no effect.

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:10.390
It's been rendered completely useless!

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:23.060
Use the Almadel.

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:24.770
Almadel?

00:15:27.140 --> 00:15:29.480
Almadel... you say?

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:30.320
Yes.

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:36.620
The virus that Prof. Kanno developed?

00:15:37.340 --> 00:15:38.970
That's incomplete!

00:15:38.970 --> 00:15:41.370
Using it without her here is dangerous!

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:43.210
No matter. Do it.

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:46.020
Understood.

00:15:46.890 --> 00:15:48.010
Loading Almadel!

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:06.610
What the?

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:09.040
Their movements are sloppy.

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:09.790
Hibiki.

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:10.490
Yes?

00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:14.740
This is about all we
can do to buy you time.

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:17.620
The rest is up to you.

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:19.300
Hibiki.

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:23.660
I... have to protect
everyone. I have to win!

00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:27.420
Enemy intrusion has reached Layer 8!

00:16:27.850 --> 00:16:30.810
We're fine so long as he
doesn't reach the heart.

00:16:30.810 --> 00:16:32.190
Stop him here.

00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:34.820
Beginning Layer 8 program copy.

00:16:34.820 --> 00:16:36.250
Disrupting the enemy!

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:44.120
That's the culprit, huh?

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:46.700
We have to hurry and get
him, or everyone...!

00:16:48.710 --> 00:16:49.780
Him, huh?

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:51.830
My ogre can...

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:53.510
Ogre!

00:16:54.630 --> 00:16:56.300
Get that person!

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:05.500
What the?!

00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:11.560
Nitta!

00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:13.150
The heck is that?

00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:16.440
Wh-What do I do?

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:22.990
Nitta!

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:33.170
Dumbass! Standin' around slack-jawed.

00:17:33.170 --> 00:17:34.070
Thank you.

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:36.280
Don't be thankin' me!

00:17:38.510 --> 00:17:40.000
Thank goodness, Nitta.

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:43.830
Hinako! Huh?

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:45.040
That's the culprit, huh?

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:50.620
Fumi Kanno?!

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:53.420
What. What's goin' on?

00:17:54.060 --> 00:17:55.630
So it's Prof. Kanno?!

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:58.180
She's brainwashed by the enemy.

00:17:58.690 --> 00:18:02.100
For the person who built JP's systems to be
the culprit...

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.000
There's no way to stop her.

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:06.480
Hibiki. Secure the cracker.

00:18:06.950 --> 00:18:08.780
Sir. Byakko!

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:18.500
Lightning won't work on that thing?

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:19.990
In that case, shockwave!

00:18:27.220 --> 00:18:27.920
Lilim!

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:31.170
What is that thing? It's so strong!

00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:33.630
Keita!

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:35.730
Let's attack at once.

00:18:35.730 --> 00:18:38.410
Huh? You tryin' to order me?

00:18:38.820 --> 00:18:40.940
Your Berserk's about at its limit.

00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:43.930
Let's finish it at once!

00:18:46.070 --> 00:18:47.310
I got no choice, huh?

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:50.690
Daichi, you listening?

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:53.120
Yeah. Yeah...

00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:55.690
Okay, got it.

00:18:57.920 --> 00:19:00.590
She's reached Azathoth,
the final line of defense!

00:19:02.460 --> 00:19:04.290
Okay. Go, Byakko!

00:19:11.720 --> 00:19:13.260
That's a decoy!

00:19:21.730 --> 00:19:22.900
Gotcha!

00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:23.470
Daichi!

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:35.080
Is it... over?

00:19:45.130 --> 00:19:47.880
That's that. Go get her.

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:53.930
It seems you've rejoiced prematurely.

00:19:56.770 --> 00:19:57.630
Berserk!

00:19:57.850 --> 00:20:00.510
Humans are naïve about follow-through.

00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:02.760
Oh, no. Run for it!

00:20:25.210 --> 00:20:27.830
Fumi Kanno. Excellent work.

00:20:28.430 --> 00:20:30.040
Now then, your final task.

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:53.910
Almadel has restarted!

00:20:56.120 --> 00:20:57.470
What does this mean?

00:21:00.250 --> 00:21:03.460
Almadel is eroding our systems!

00:21:03.460 --> 00:21:07.410
This is system-breaking code,
designed to erase any traces of the user.

00:21:10.720 --> 00:21:12.930
The firewall is completely down.

00:21:15.260 --> 00:21:18.130
Infiltration rate: 100%.

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:21.880
Tsutenkaku's defensive barrier
has been eliminated.

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:24.580
It's terrible.

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:39.660
I'm... alive?

00:21:43.750 --> 00:21:46.130
It's a sliding safe...

00:21:54.720 --> 00:21:56.760
Keita? Keita!

00:21:56.760 --> 00:21:57.810
Keita!

00:21:58.720 --> 00:21:59.710
No!

00:21:59.710 --> 00:22:01.310
It can't be!

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:04.350
He's dead!

00:22:05.620 --> 00:22:09.150
We couldn't prevent that
"dead face" footage.

00:22:10.280 --> 00:22:12.450
And we knew it what would happen!

00:22:13.640 --> 00:22:17.730
Spiritual defense capabilities for
the Osaka area... are zero.

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:20.450
Septentrion have appeared in Osaka!

00:24:03.100 --> 00:24:06.350
The objective is Osaka's
